//@version=5
// visual_relativeMeasuredVolatility
// Best-effort reconstruction of DeepVue's "Relative Measured Volatility"
// (RMV): flags volatility-contraction bars with a white dot below the
// candle, for spotting VCP-style tightening. DeepVue's exact formula is
// proprietary/undisclosed; this implements only what's publicly
// documented on deepvue.com:
//   - raw high-low range per bar
//   - down-weighted on below-average volume
//   - normalized (percentile rank) against the prior N bars, excluding
//     the current bar, onto a 0-100 scale (0 = tightest, 100 = most
//     volatile)
// See visual_relativeMeasuredVolatility.txt for the full writeup and the
// specific assumptions made where the public spec is silent.
indicator("visual_relativeMeasuredVolatility", overlay=true, max_bars_back=50)

// ---- Inputs ----
lookback     = input.int(15, "Normalization lookback", options=[5, 10, 15, 20])
volAvgLength = input.int(30, "Volume average length")
tightThresh  = input.int(20, "Tight threshold (0-100, <=)", minval=0, maxval=100)

// ---- 1. Raw bar range ----
barRange = high - low

// ---- 2. Volume down-weighting ----
// Below-average volume scales the range down proportionally (half of
// average volume counts for half its range); above-average volume is
// not boosted, weight caps at 1.0.
volAvg = ta.sma(volume, volAvgLength)
volWeight = volume < volAvg ? volume / volAvg : 1.0
weightedRange = barRange * volWeight

// ---- 3. Percentile-rank normalization vs the prior `lookback` bars, ----
// excluding the current bar. Done manually (not ta.percentrank) because
// that built-in includes the current bar in its comparison window.
count = 0.0
for i = 1 to lookback
    if weightedRange[i] < weightedRange
        count += 1

rmv = count / lookback * 100.0

// ---- 4. Tightness flag + visualization ----
isTight = rmv <= tightThresh
plotshape(isTight, style=shape.circle, location=location.belowbar, color=color.white, size=size.tiny, title="Tight (RMV)")

// Raw value exposed to the Data Window only, for tuning against a real
// DeepVue chart or against the RTI indicator, without drawing on the
// price chart's scale.
plot(rmv, title="RMV Value", display=display.data_window)
